This one took a while, considering that I didn't polypile or pudding farm it 
took way longer than it should have... I once again wasted a lot of time 
searching for Vlad's tower.  I was Magic Mapping and Detecting Treasure and 
had the bad luck for a pet to drop something on the stairs.  They were two 
steps from the upstairs on Baal's level (in the wrong direction of course.)
Random selection gave me an elven wizard who started with: +oForce Bolt, 
Charm Monster and Create Monster, /oCancellation (no bag surprises) and =oSD 
so this one had a very easy early game.  Rolled int of 20 made PW a non 
issue after a level or two.  I got Magicbane before entering the mines 
(altar on DL2) and hit minetown to find two magic lamps (SDSM and my 
permanent light source) a magic whistle and a cross aligned temple.  I 
wandered to the level below minetown (it was lit) and stumbled across a 
polytrap.  Puss Puss became a glass golem on the first whistle-in and would 
be with me till the sanctum.  He beat many a shopkeeper to death and after I 
had donated several times would get me a refund from the minetown priest 
later.  On the way back up an orc dropped another helm, it turned out to be 
+4!  Sokoban had the bag I needed badly by then (I really don't like being 
restricted to St18 and Co16)  My starting wand made water creation easy so I 
had !oHW already.  Puss Puss whacked a unicorn in the zoo so I blessed a 
horn as well.  Back to the mines for more RNG goodness, I charmed a Vampire 
lord and got several books in the haunted library.  I did have to hand write 
+oMagic Missile around here but I had found two markers to add to the one I 
started with so it was all good.   I set up my first stash at the altar on 
dl2 and went on a sac fest to max my luck and get another couple of spell 
books.  I accidentally over sacrificed and got gifted with Giantslayer.  I 
would regret this later wasting three wishes on trying to get the MKoT.  The 
only other artifact I generated was Excalibur in one of my own bones files: 
a knight who made it as far as DL12 before his pet polyed into a master lich 
and turned invisible to be bumped into.  The ingrate promptly used the touch 
of death on the hapless knight.  A sad, sad end.

There was no sign of ludious, though I did dig out all the vaults for 
protection money.  I'd get to naked AC of 1 but never could get that lower 
even though there was another temple in the main dungeon and the priest in 
the valley.  I finished enchanting my gear at the castle, using Drain Life 
to make sure I got +5 on everything.  The demon lords were a pain with only 
MM and MB for offense although my pet glass golem did attack them after I 
wore them down a bit.  Orcus didn't manage to empty his wand (stunned by MB) 
and my trusty towel prevented Baal from being to much of a headache.  I 
charmed a few Umber Hulks (as many as three at one time) who dug out 
portions of several levels for me (no +oDig till Rodney dropped his on 
Earth) Rodney's tower was ~DL 43 the fakewiz was 47 and the VS was on 49. 
After finally locating Vlad's tower I got my one and only "oLS (worn to the 
demibar) I then dropped off the Candleabrum and Bell and portaled back to 
the castle then Levelported back to my second stash on DL13 for a sacfest 
and Alchemy session. I got my HP's up to ~250 at this point (from 150) and 
wrote several ?oCharging which I confused myself and read to get my PW to 
~350  The eye brought me back to Vlad's and I Levelported back to dl47 to 
borrow Rodney's book. The tower was routine and the sanctum started up 
promisingly with a cockatrice showing up at the exit from the graveyard. 
It's corpse allowed me to spare the finger for a while while wading in after 
it rotted away (yes it took that many turns) I got into some trouble I 
didn't have enough firepower to kill a nalfeshnee (or was it an ice devil?) 
before it started gating in hell-p including Yeenoghu and a horde of 
assorted demons.  Puss Puss gave his all during this summoning storm and the 
Demon lord managed to whack the high priest of moloch so I had to get the 
amulet from him.  Another yellow c provided the offense I was missing and I 
left the demon horde to their own devices (c!oGL)

The mysterious force was gentle, only hitting me three times, and only once 
backtracking.  I had controlled teleportitis so getting around wasn't hard. 
The planes weren't too scary, Earth had the portal at the top right of the 
screen, Air saw the liberal use of the Finger as well as magic mapping to 
find a clear path through the cloudbank.  For Fire I changed into Vlad's WWB 
(fireproofed +5) and took the long walk to the portal (top left) water was 
it's usual bore, I changed back into my speed boots and took the time to 
read a ?oCharging after my ?oGD to mark the portal so I entered the Astral 
plane with full PW and ~12 /oDeath zaps.  I'd need them, famine and pesty 
were annoyingly persistant in trying to get to meele range  I avoided 
death's branch and it proved to be the right move to go left. (after trying 
the center branch that is.)

One of the player monsters (tourist) on astral was almost on top of me when 
I entered and ended up being made peaceful by my charming of the crowd 
summoned by a master lich.  The rogue on my kill list blocked my entrance to 
the high temple and succumbed to MB of all things.  He was armed with a 
vanilla longsword according to an insightful probe.

